h('How I directed the use of OpenAI')
p('I supplied OpenAI Codex with the assignment and a structured prompt directing it to read the requirements, define minimal established concepts, describe attributes/actions and relationships, cite sources, and produce a 5-10-page conceptual report. I specified use cases, simulated trading and explicit assumptions, and instructed it not to invent lecture content or team details.')
p('My later instructions covered implementation, tests, debugging and preserved evidence. I requested a clearer frontend, supplied the stock files and lecture screenshots, and asked for reported failures to be fixed. The original prompt and actual follow-ups are distinguished from summaries of AI-directed work in the development log.')
h('AI contribution and verification')
p('AI helped interpret requirements, organize the financial concepts, map their relationships, and later generate code and tests. I supplied the assignment, detailed prompts, lecture screenshots and stock files; I also reported failing tests and requested corrections. The preserved record does not establish an independent human audit, so automated checks are identified separately from my inputs.')
p('Recorded checks include opening definition sources, validating the 20 CSV files and their dates, rendering the PDF, and running the build and 56 Jasmine tests successfully. Small expected results were checked against explicit arithmetic: $100 minus 3 shares at $12.50 leaves $62.50. A browser save/cancel check left cash unchanged. AI-generated tests still required review: safe retries during a provider outage and basket timestamp consistency needed corrections after earlier tests passed. Evidence and versions are retained in the development log.')
p('Before submission, the team should independently confirm the financial definitions, selected calculations, lecture alignment and scope. No independent human verification or future investment performance is claimed where it has not been recorded. The full initiating prompt remains in evidence/reference-request.txt.')


